# DATABASE MIGRATION STRATEGY

# Migration Philosophy

Database schema changes must:

* be version-controlled
* be reversible
* be tested before production
* never manually alter production data

---

# Migration Tool

Recommended:

* golang-migrate

---

# Migration Structure

```text id="07w0w7"
migrations/
    000001_create_users.up.sql
    000001_create_users.down.sql
```

---

# Migration Rules

* one logical change per migration
* all migrations reversible
* never edit executed migrations
* create new migrations instead

---

# Deployment Strategy

Deployment flow:

```text id="wxk8eq"
Deploy Application
↓
Run Migrations
↓
Validate Health Checks
↓
Enable Traffic
```

---

# Rollback Strategy

If deployment fails:

* rollback application
* rollback migration if safe
* restore backup if necessary

---

# Backup Policy

Before production migrations:

* automatic DB backup required

---

# Schema Evolution Principles

Avoid:

* breaking existing APIs
* destructive column removals
* long-running table locks

Prefer:

* additive changes
* staged migrations
* backward compatibility

---

# Production Safety Rules

NEVER:

* manually edit production tables
* bypass migration tooling
* run untested migrations
